r+=['','## 3. Rotation, bench depth and availability','', 'Actual rotation selection prioritizes natural positions and depth coverage, then stamina, planned minutes, foul trouble, workload, coaching and closing/garbage-time context. A natural-position preference can outweigh small OVR differences. Injured players are excluded; emergency fallback does not make injured or disqualified players eligible. Managed workload restrictions are honored subject to having enough available players.','', 'Shallow/deep tests change only the away bench attributes (−15/+10 bounded rating points, excluding height). They are deliberately strong sensitivity probes, not realistic population estimates. The starters-versus-balanced probe gives home starters +5 and home bench −10. Short-long restricts only the home planned rotation; actual substitutions remain free to respond to stamina/positions. No production rotation rule was changed merely to erase the value of depth.','', 'The original NBA injured diagnostic had an incorrect fixture timestamp and is retained under excluded-fixtures/, omitted from every reported result. It was rerun with a validated medicalInfo.until and an explicit injuryDays assertion. The WNBA setup error was corrected before accepted quality-model data were generated. Failed/incomplete season processes were retried, not counted.','', '## 4. Controlled experiments','', 'Baseline fixtures use Phase 3 mechanics. Candidate fixtures use the exact two mechanics changes. Rosters, bios, personality identity, coaching and rest are matched unless the scenario intentionally changes them. Four roster templates are reused in blocks of 50; sample uncertainty does not cover every possible roster. Standard neutral/home cases set one rest day, full starting energy, no rivalry and no altitude. High/low crowd changes attendance and energy; altitude uses 5,280 feet. Each row retains complete raw outcomes.','','| Case | N | Pts/team | Mean margin | Signed margin SD | Abs margin SD | Home win % | ≤10 % | 20+ % | 30+ % | 40+ % | FG% | 3P% |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for k,m in sorted(c.items()):r.append('| '+k+' | '+' | '.join(f'{m[z]:.2f}'for z in ['n','points','meanMargin','marginSD','absoluteMarginSD','homeWin%','close10%','blow20','blow30','blow40','FG%','3P%'])+' |')
r+=['','“no-three-contest” is the retained filename for neutralizing the base three-point defensive rating at 75. It does NOT disable every contest penalty. “no-fatigue” removes effective-attribute fatigue reductions, not stamina-driven substitutions. “no-physical” removes derived attributes and direct matchup bonuses, not every biography-based rebound factor. These are bounded ablations, not complete system removal. controlled-comparisons.json includes paired mean-absolute-margin deltas and 95% intervals against the neutral fixture (or the matching baseline for candidate cases); intervals crossing zero do not establish a reliable improvement.','', '## 5. Home-court effects','', 'The crowd system adds home shooting probability, subtracts road shooting probability, changes foul risk, adds a small road turnover hazard, affects rebound odds and produces bounded home momentum. Those paths are cumulative by design, not literally duplicate applications of the same function. Their combined modern effect was too large relative to matched-roster tests and both recent official reference seasons.','', 'The candidate multiplies the existing crowd scale by 0.6 for simulation years 2023 onward, preserving the home-advantage setting and venue differences. This is an empirical modern calibration, NOT an assertion that a league rule changed in 2023. Earlier years retain their existing magnitude. Altitude, rivalry and rest mechanisms are untouched.','', 'There is also an existing two-day-rest asymmetry: +1 passing for either team, but +2 defensive awareness/rebounding only for the home team. The rest-neutral2/rest-home2 probes isolate that behavior; rest-unequal compares two home rest days with one away. This remains an explicit home-preparation modeling assumption, not silently removed or counted as a crowd fix.','', '| Matched comparison | N | Mean home-margin change | Approximate paired 95% interval |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for l in ['nba','wnba']:
 for va,sa,vb,sb in [('baseline','home','baseline','neutral'),('candidate','home','candidate','neutral'),('candidate','home','baseline','home')]:
  a=json.load(open(p/f'{va}-{l}-{sa}.json'))['games'];b=json.load(open(p/f'{vb}-{l}-{sb}.json'))['games'];ds=[(x['score'][0]-x['score'][1])-(y['score'][0]-y['score'][1])for x,y in zip(a,b)];mu=st.mean(ds);h=1.96*st.stdev(ds)/len(ds)**.5;r.append(f'| {l} {va}/{sa} minus {vb}/{sb} | {len(ds)} | {mu:+.2f} | {mu-h:+.2f} to {mu+h:+.2f} |')
r+=['','The paired intervals describe these fixtures; sequential random branches diverge after a changed play. They are not possession-for-possession counterfactual estimates. Home/away scoring, turnovers, foul counts, shooting attempts and recorded player stamina totals (not mean energy percentages) are retained in controlled-summary.json.','', '## 6. Three-point shooting','', 'Confirmed defect: attributes.js could assign contest=true to transition/drive-and-kick decisions that explicitly carried openLook=true. The contest expression now honors the open-look flag before the generic random contest branch. In 30 baseline games, 316 of 1,951 open decisions received a contest; in 30 candidate games, zero of 1,997 did. Changed counts reflect divergent random branches, not invented shots. This corrects primary-shot context, not every secondary-shot situation.','', 'The remaining accuracy gap cannot be attributed solely to this bug. The base shot formula, shooter/defender differences, contested and self-created penalties, tendencies, coaching, morale, physical matchup and fatigue all remain active. No universal three-point bonus was added. The actual season 3P results above determine whether the defect correction materially closes the population-level gap.','', '## 7. Efficiency, roster distribution and shared pace','', 'Team-season distributions use a common estimate: FGA − ORB + total turnovers + 0.44 FTA, averaged between opponents for each game. This is not exact ball-control pace; foul mix and team rebounds can differ. Simulated team-seasons pool ten leagues, so their extrema should not be equated with one real season’s extrema.','', '| Population | Team-seasons | ORtg SD | DRtg SD | Net rating SD | Net p10 | Net p90 | Opposing score correlation | Shared estimated-pace SD |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for l in ['nba','wnba']:
 for phase in ['phase3','phase4']:
  e=s[l][phase]['efficiency'];t=e['teamSeason'];r.append(f"| {l} {phase} | {e['teams']} | {t['ORtg']['sd']:.2f} | {t['DRtg']['sd']:.2f} | {t['net']['sd']:.2f} | {t['net']['p10']:.2f} | {t['net']['p90']:.2f} | {e['scoreCorrelation']:.3f} | {e['sharedEstimatedPace']['sd']:.2f} |")
for name,e in refs.items():
 t=e['teamSeason'];r.append(f"| {name} official | {e['teams']} | {t['ORtg']['sd']:.2f} | {t['DRtg']['sd']:.2f} | {t['net']['sd']:.2f} | {t['net']['p10']:.2f} | {t['net']['p90']:.2f} | {e['scoreCorrelation']:.3f} | {e['sharedEstimatedPace']['sd']:.2f} |")
r+=['','The Phase 3 WNBA net-rating SD is below both real reference seasons even while blowouts are too frequent. The NBA SD is broadly similar to its references. This does not prove every fictional roster is realistic, but it contradicts an explanation based only on excessive league-wide roster separation. No roster generator change was justified. Healthy minutes-weighted quality, bench-share, attribute and energy distributions for the separate 8-seed population are in quality-analysis.json. Expansion talent concentration and long-term free-agency concentration were not independently calibrated in this phase.','', 'Both clubs already share the same scheduled possession-window count: the engine uses both coaches’ tempos, the user’s pace if involved, a shared random pace term, rest workload and the historical pace multiplier. Fast-fast/fast-slow probes test this directly. The engine is still a fixed-window approximation; repeated rebounds and retained foul possessions can be compressed into a window. The lower simulated opposing-score correlation is a remaining modeling signal, not proof that a hidden score-correlation bonus would be valid. No artificial shared shooting multiplier was added.','', 'Detailed per-team ORtg, DRtg, net rating, eFG, opponent eFG, turnover rate, offensive-rebound share and FT rate distributions, plus team-game FG/3P/eFG/TS and score variance/covariance, are retained in summary.json and reference-analysis.json.','', '## 8. Fourth-quarter development','', '| League / phase | Mean halftime margin | Mean Q4-entry margin | Mean final margin | Q4 trailer eventually wins % | Bench minutes/team | Garbage-time game % |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for l in ['nba','wnba']:
 for phase in ['phase3','phase4']:
  a=s[l][phase]['aggregate'];d=s[l][phase]['development'];r.append(f"| {l} {phase} | {d['marginAfter2']['mean']:.2f} | {d['marginAfter3']['mean']:.2f} | {a['meanMargin']:.2f} | {a['Q4trailerWins%']:.2f} | {d['benchMinutes']:.2f} | {d['garbageGames%']:.2f} |")
r+=['','Margin-conditioned late-game results are included in summary.json. They are observational: a 20-point lead selects teams already performing better. The code already switches to bench-prioritized rotations in late blowouts and uses closing lineups in close games. There is no generic lead-based shooting boost; crowd momentum is bounded and was included in the crowd-scale reduction. These data do not justify a trailing-team boost. Exact real-game quarter-by-quarter and intentional-foul rate calibration was not newly completed in this phase.','', '## 9. Historical and regression verification','', '150 full-length games across NBA 1997/2025 and WNBA 1997/2006/2024 verify formats, nonnegative box statistics, shot bounds and final score/summary agreement. The inaugural WNBA retains two 20-minute halves; later WNBA uses four 10-minute quarters; NBA uses four 12-minute quarters. Overtime remains five minutes. These are format/regression checks with fictional rosters, not statistically verified historical competitiveness calibration.','', 'All 14,700 accepted full-season games are checked for exact per-team game counts, balanced home/away totals, no same-day conflicts, player-minutes totals, period scores, final scores, box-score scoring identities and player-versus-team turnover accounting. The 40 actual Player Feat regression games cover event provenance, live/final distinction, deterministic replay, completed-game recognition and save/reload publication idempotence; synthetic cases also cover overtime winners, buzzer timing and Finals context. A Phase 3 save retains completed scores, boxes and summary events under the candidate.','', 'Thirty fatigued-game regressions preserve permanent attributes and secondary-shot calculations; 26 foul regressions preserve technical/flagrant event and box totals; 1,361 defender-attribute accesses retain correct current-defender stamina. The additional projection and home-court regression outputs are retained alongside these tests. No browser layout change is made. Browser rendering itself is not revalidated by these engine tests.','', '## 10. Files and reproduction','', 'Production: dist/attributes.js (open-look contest correction), dist/home-court.js (modern crowd scale), dist/index.html (cache-key refresh). Documentation: docs/PHASE4-COMPETITIVENESS.md and dist/audits/phase4.html. Diagnostics: dev/audit-competitiveness.cjs (Phase 4 run claims only), dev/phase4-*.cjs/.py, dev/run-phase4-*.cjs, dev/rotation-quality-diagnostic.js, dev/test-phase4-*.cjs, dev/verify-phase4.py. Data: dev/phase4/ and dev/balance-audit/phase4-*.json. No save schema or database migration is required.','', 'Reproduce full seasons: node dev/run-phase4-seasons.cjs. It skips completed output files and uses bounded-memory workers; remove only Phase 4 output files in a separate checkout to rerun. Candidate transforms read preserved Phase 3 source, so they remain reproducible after production publication. Diagnostics: node dev/run-phase4-diagnostics.cjs; candidate controls: node dev/run-phase4-candidate-controls.cjs; additional rotation/rest/tempo probes: node dev/run-phase4-extra.cjs. Model: node dev/run-phase4-quality.cjs, then python3 dev/phase4-fit-quality.py and python3 dev/phase4-quality-analysis.py. Analysis: python3 dev/phase4-analysis.py; integrity: python3 dev/verify-phase4.py.','', 'Baseline-hashes.json preserves all original production files, city photos, Phase 2/3 season data and previous Phase 3 JSON outputs. Only explicitly listed production paths are exempted after applying the tested changes.','', '## Remaining limitations','', '- Excessive blowouts and low three-point accuracy remain; compare every tail and scoring metric rather than declaring success from home wins alone.','- The prediction model is experimental and does not replace historical spreads, displayed ratings, playoff odds or AI valuations.','- Historical crowd magnitudes, expansion-roster distributions, long-term free-agency concentration and exact real-game rotation strategies remain uncalibrated.','- Fixed possession windows, incomplete team-rebound accounting and a generic possession estimator limit causal pace conclusions.','- Home-only two-day-rest preparation remains a documented assumption; it is not confused with the crowd fix.','- The reference samples and four held-out roster seeds are finite. Zero rare events and small prediction gains are not proof of exact probabilities or broad generalization.','']
text='\n'.join(r);pathlib.Path('docs/PHASE4-COMPETITIVENESS.md').write_text(text)
# Portable report with readable tables, no external assets or scripts.
def render_report(lines):
 chunks=[];table=False;listing=False
 for line in lines:
  if not line.startswith('|') and table:chunks.append('</tbody></table>');table=False
  if not line.startswith('- ') and listing:chunks.append('</ul>');listing=False
  if line.startswith('|'):
   cells=[html.escape(v.strip())for v in line.strip('|').split('|')]
   if all(set(v)<=set('-: ')for v in cells):continue
   tag='td' if table else 'th'
   if not table:chunks.append('<table><tbody>');table=True
   chunks.append('<tr>'+''.join('<'+tag+'>'+v+'</'+tag+'>'for v in cells)+'</tr>')
  elif line.startswith('#'):
   n=len(line)-len(line.lstrip('#'));chunks.append('<h'+str(n)+'>'+html.escape(line[n:].strip())+'</h'+str(n)+'>')
  elif line.startswith('- '):
   if not listing:chunks.append('<ul>');listing=True
   chunks.append('<li>'+html.escape(line[2:])+'</li>')
  elif line:chunks.append('<p>'+html.escape(line)+'</p>')
 if table:chunks.append('</tbody></table>')
 if listing:chunks.append('</ul>')
 return ''.join(chunks)
body=render_report(r)
pathlib.Path('dist/audits').mkdir(exist_ok=True);pathlib.Path('dist/audits/phase4.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hoops Dynasty — Phase 4 Audit</title><style>body{background:#111820;color:#e6e9ec;font:16px/1.65 system-ui;margin:0;padding:32px;max-width:1300px;margin:auto}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.2;color:#f6c477}h2{margin-top:2.5em}a{color:#ffac72}table{display:block;overflow:auto;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin:20px 0}td,th{padding:8px 12px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #3a4651;white-space:nowrap}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}p,li{max-width:1000px}</style>'+body+'</html>')
print('Wrote report',len(text),'characters')
